L81: Server Side. At the initialization phase, the server trains a supervised global model on the public labeled dataset $\mathcal{D}_{p}$ and a high-capacity teacher model on the same dataset. While any high-performance model could serve as the teacher in our framework, we adopt SAM for its strong generalization capability, denoted as $\mathcal{M}_{T}$.
L82: We fine-tune SAM on the server side using the labeled dataset and Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA), and then distribute the resulting teacher model, along with the public labeled dataset $\mathcal{D}_{p}$, to all clients for pseudo-supervision. On each client, this teacher distills knowledge into a lightweight semi-supervised model through an adaptive, agreement-driven mechanism.
L83: Algorithm 1 SAM-Fed Training
L84: 
L85: Server side
L86: 
L87: Input : Public dataset $\mathcal{D}_{p}$, SAM teacher $\mathcal{M}_{T}$, global model $\mathcal{M}_{G}$
L88: 
L89: Fine-tune $\mathcal{M}_{T}$ on $\mathcal{D}_{p}$, Train $\mathcal{M}_{G}$ on $\mathcal{D}_{p}$
L90: 
L91: Broadcast the weights of $\mathcal{M}_{T}$ and $\mathcal{D}_{p}$ to all clients
L92: 
L93: Client side
L94: 
L95: Input : Public dataset $\mathcal{D}_{p}$, local unlabeled dataset $\mathcal{D}^{U}_{c}$, client model $\mathcal{M}_{c}$, $\mathcal{D}^{PL}_{c}=\varnothing$
L96: Train local model $\mathcal{M}_{c}$ on $\mathcal{D}_{p}$
L97: 
L98: for $\mathbf{x}_{j}^{c}\in\mathcal{D}^{U}_{c}$ do
L99: 
L100:      Generate pseudo-labels using $\mathcal{M}_{T}$ and $\mathcal{M}_{c}$
L101: 
L102:      Generate pixel-wise agreement mask using the Adaptive Agreement Mechanism $\triangleright$ Eqs. (cite35†1 )–(cite36†2 )
L103: 
L104:      Compute confidence weights $\lambda_{j}$ for each pixel $\triangleright$ Eqs. (cite37†3 )
L105: 
L106:      $\mathcal{D}^{PL}_{c}\leftarrow\acute{y}_{j},\lambda_{j}$
L107: Train $\mathcal{M}_{c}$ on $\mathcal{D}^{PL}_{c}$ using confidence-weighted consistency loss.
L108: 
L109: Apply federated aggregation.
