L165:  | $$\mathbf{R}^{(l)}=\mathbf{R}^{(l-1)}-\mathbf{Q}^{(l)}.$$  |  | (12)
L166: 
L167: The primary objective is to minimize the reconstruction loss between the original embeddings and their quantized representations. For input embeddings $\mathbf{X}$, we apply a combination of absolute reconstruction losses with Eq. cite85†13 .
L168:  | $$\mathcal{L}_{\text{recon}}=\|\mathbf{{X}}-\sum_{l=1}^{L}\mathbf{{Q}}^{(l)}\|_{2}^{2}.$$  |  | (13)
L169: 
L170: To promote balanced utilization of the learned clusters and prevent cluster collapse, we introduce an entropy-based regularization term. For each layer $l$, the cluster usage distribution is computed as shown in Eq. cite86†14 .
L171: 
L172:  | $$p_{k}^{(l)}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{I}[\mathbf{z}_{i}^{(l)}=k],$$  |  | (14)
L173: where $\mathbb{I}[\cdot]$ is the indicator function. The regularization loss encourages uniform cluster usage through KL divergence:
L174: 
L175:  | $$\mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}}^{(l)}=\text{KL}\left(p^{(l)}\|\mathbf{u}\right)=\sum_{k=1}^{K_{l}}p_{k}^{(l)}\log\frac{p_{k}^{(l)}}{1/K_{l}},$$  |  | (15)
L176: 
L177: where $\mathbf{u}=[1/K_{l},\ldots,1/K_{l}]$ represents the uniform distribution over $K_{l}$ clusters. The complete training objective combines reconstruction with cluster usage regularization:
L178:  | $$\mathcal{L}_{\text{HGIT}}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{recon}}+\lambda_{\text{reg}}\sum_{l=2}^{L}\mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}}^{(l)},$$  |  | (16)
L179: 
L180: where $\lambda_{\text{reg}}$ controls the strength of the regularization. Note that regularization is only applied to learnable layers ($l\geq 2$) since the first layer uses pre-computed geographic clusters.
L181: ## Experiment
L182: 
L183: In this section, we conduct extensive experiments on real-world datasets to address the following research questions:
L184: 
L185:   * •
L186: 
L187: RQ1: How does LGSID improve upon existing tokenization for SOTA discriminative and generative models?
L188: 
L189:   * •
L190: 
L191: RQ2: How does fine-tuning affect the LLM’s ability on enhancing geographic awareness while preserving semantic understanding?
L192: 
L193:   * •
L194: 
L195: RQ3: How accurately do item representations and quantized IDs reflect real-world geographic proximity?
L196: 
L197:   * •
L198: RQ4: How does LGSID exhibit superior geographic awareness compared to other SID methods?
L199: ### Experiment Settings
L200: 
L201: The datsets and evaluation, finetune settings, parameters settings and baseline models are detailed in Appendix: B.
